SQLite is in the public domain.

The SQLite source code, including the sqlite3.h header that sqlite3.ti is translated from
and the library built or downloaded into lib/, carries no copyright: its authors dedicated it
to the public domain. See https://sqlite.org/copyright.html.

The header comment of sqlite3.h reads, in place of a legal notice:

    May you do good and not evil.
    May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
    May you share freely, never taking more than you give.
